    "event": "Small Craft Advisory",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Tiyan GU",
    "headline": "Small Craft Advisory issued November 24 at 4:53PM ChST until November 25 at 5:00AM ChST by NWS Tiyan GU",
    "description": "* WHAT...East to northeast winds 10 to 15 kt with frequent gusts up\nto 25 kt.\n\n* WHERE...Marianas Coastal Waters.\n\n* WHEN...Until 5 AM ChST Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Conditions will be hazardous to small craft.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Today's airport observations and scatterometry\npaired with model guidance suggests frequent gusts exceeding the\nSmall Craft Advisory threshold of 22 knots continuing through\ntonight. Winds will briefly drop Wednesday before a trade-wind\nsurge potentially develops over the region, which could continue\nthe Small Craft Advisory beyond Wednesday.",
    "instruction": "Inexperienced mariners, especially those operating smaller vessels,\nshould avoid boating in hazardous conditions.",
    "response": "Avoid",
    "note": null,
    "parameters": {
